      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Auth0 for Federated User**\n\nOkay, I'm zeroing in on Auth0 as the external provider for fetching and normalizing claims. It's a solid choice given its popularity and federated user capabilities. I'm focusing on ensuring its identifier is correctly integrated within the `profile_claims.py` script.\n\n\n**Defining Claims and Code**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Auth0, focusing on creating the `profile_claims.py` file. I've included a placeholder for `AUTH0_DOMAIN` to clearly signal Auth0 as the provider. I'm now drafting the simulated `fetch_claims_from_auth0` and `normalize_claims` functions within the file, followed by a demonstrative main block.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789862164655,
          "start": 1789862161191
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc192b27001CWFhoUk43tf2xV",
